From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:57:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: persist effective prompt and tool definition snapshots

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: persist effective request prompts and tools alongside assistant replies
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none

Patch intent:
Capture the exact combined system text and common tool definitions passed
to blocking and streaming provider requests. Independently deduplicate each
value per session and reference it from the successful assistant response.

Why it exists:
Session analysis needs to recover the request context associated with a
response and its tool calls. Persist only common tool definitions, not
provider-specific wire forms, credentials, or execution results.

Upstream integration points:
ToolDefinition in jcode-message-types, Agent::run_turn and
run_turn_streaming_mpsc, Session::messages and persistence journal.

Update guidance:
Keep prompt and definition equality collision-safe and independently
deduplicated. Capture the concatenated static and dynamic prompt plus the
full effective tool definitions immediately before `complete_split` in both
blocking and streaming paths. Associate snapshots only after an assistant
response is recorded; do not persist prewarm-only or failed provider attempts.

Message references are indexes into per-session prompt and tool tables. Keep
the tables and references aligned through journal replay, checkpoint/save,
resume, session forks, transcript replacement, and compaction. When transcript
replacement discards messages, clear or retain the associated tables
consistently. Preserve references on surviving stored assistant messages.
Compaction creates a provider-facing summary view: capture the rebuilt request
for its response, without confusing that view with removal of stored messages.

Store the common tool definition's name, description, and input schema. Do not
substitute configured tool names or provider-specific wire serialization,
credentials, MCP authorization headers, or tool outputs.

Storage measurement:
The request_snapshots_deduplicate_independently_and_survive_persistence test
serializes a representative 300-line system prompt, 20 tool definitions, and
100 message references as 19,792 bytes when values are shared. Repeating the
full prompt and definitions in every message takes 1,748,701 bytes in the same
JSON-size comparison. This is a fixture measurement, not a universal session
size prediction: real schema and prompt sizes vary, and the persisted session
also contains transcript and journal data. Keep independent deduplication and
the representative regression bound when evolving snapshot persistence.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh check -p jcode-session-types -p jcode-base -p jcode-app-core -p jcode-tui
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-session-types request_snapshot --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-base request_snapshot --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core tool_streaming --lib
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-app-core provider_request --lib
